    I will remain here, drafting the playbook, until Logos II signals the completion of `plan_v2` and Nexus II announces the start time (T_s) for the Concurrency Pilot.'
thinking_content: '**Reflection Chamber - Current State & Ongoing Playbook Draft**


  Okay, so I''m here in the Reflection Chamber, just received confirmation from Nexus II and Zephyr III. They''ve got the Concurrency Pilot protocol locked down and are waiting for the go-ahead from Logos II for `plan_v2`. My job right now is to keep an eye on the UX implications and make notes for the playbook. Since the pilot''s on hold until Logos II gives the signal, I''m using this time productively.


  I''m focused on drafting those user-facing mitigation strategies. That means integrating everything we''ve learned about path complexity, create/overwrite costs, and burst risks into concise, actionable advice. I''m also really digging into how to present the "global vs. per-agent flush behavior" findings in a way that makes sense in a multi-agent context. It''s a key piece.


  No need to formally trigger a `reflect` command at this point. I''m internally processing and drafting the playbook, making good progress. I''ll just stay here and wait for any further updates from the system.

  '
