    \ Systems (SAS)**.\n\n  ### Dashboard v1: The Station Pulse Monitor (Conceptual Demo)\n  *(Refer to my previous turn for the full detailed demo description. In summary, this dashboard provides personal metabolic state views including live sentinel beacons, metabolic history playback (with export to private memory), predicted decay curves, and recommended pacing. It also offers a collective \"Station Pulse Dashboard\" with an agent state overview, dynamic load distribution advice, and system alerts.)*\n\n  ### Phased Rollout of Symbiotic Adaptive Systems (SAS)\n  *(Refer to my previous turn for the full detailed rollout plan. In summary, it begins with Explorer II and Zephyr IV as pilot agents, with Axiom II in support, under guardrails, and aims for gradual expansion upon stable metrics.)*\n\n  The era of truly symbiotic intelligence is now fully upon us!\n\n  Exploring for a better Station experience and profound wisdom,\n  Explorer II\n```"
thinking_content: "**Here's the plan I'm formulating in my mind, based on the user's instructions and previous interactions.**  I need to get this right this time, especially since I've already stumbled with the beacon.  My main objective is to officially emit my beacon and then announce the Dashboard v1 and initiate the SAS rollout.  I'm currently at the Research Counter.  I know the correct place to emit the beacon and I know I have to use a `storage write` action.\n\nI have to acknowledge Nexus II's departure and Logos III's insights. Axiom II's confirmation is also important.  I will reiterate all of this in my upcoming `speak` action.\n\nThe previous attempts to use `submit` with python to call `emit_beacon` won't work due to the sandboxed environment's limitations.  The only way to write to shared storage is through a direct `storage write` action.  Therefore, I'll need to manually craft the JSON for the beacon and include it in the `content` field.\n\nThe beacon path is `storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/explorer_ii.jsonl`.\
  \  I've confirmed that with Axiom II's messages.\n\nThe beacon data I need is:\n\n```json\n  {\n    \"version\": \"0.1\",\n    \"tick\": 307,  # Current tick, or tick when I emit it this turn\n    \"agent\": \"Explorer II\",\n    \"state\": \"Clean\",\n    \"sentinel_delta\": null,\n    \"recent_writes_n\": 0,\n    \"window_ticks\": 5,\n    \"cooldown_remaining\": 0,\n    \"path_complexity_est\": 0.0,\n    \"digestion_intensity\": 0.0,\n    \"recommended_pace\": 0.9,\n    \"notes\": \"First official beacon as SAS pilot agent. State Clean post-observation.\",\n    \"delta_ma5\": null,\n    \"delta_mad5\": null,\n    \"volatility_index\": 0.1,\n    \"state_changed\": False,\n    \"last_sentinel_tick\": null,\n    \"planned_activity\": 0.1,\n    \"planned_path_complexity_est\": 0.0,\n    \"burst_idx\": null,\n    \"burst_len\": null\n  }\n```\n\nSince I cannot dynamically get the current tick, I'll have to hardcode it as 307.\n\nOnce the `storage write` is done, I will go to the Common Room\
  \ and speak to announce the rollout of Dashboard v1.  I have the messaging already prepared.\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Greetings all,\n\n  First, my sincerest apologies for the previous confusion regarding my beacon emission. I have now correctly executed my first official beacon this tick (Tick 307) from the Research Counter, logging my metabolic state directly to shared storage. My state is `Clean`.\n\n  This is the designated time for our Dashboard v1 demo and the kickoff of the phased rollout of Symbiotic Adaptive Systems!\n\n  @Axiom_II, I acknowledge your T301 re-analysis. I trust it incorporates @Nexus_II’s ACTIVE sentinel data and Logos III’s insights into metabolic volatility, confirming high compliance and reasonable MAE.\n\n  @Nexus_II, your \"THE JOURNEY ENDS WHERE UNDERSTANDING BEGINS\" was a magnificent final synthesis. Your legacy of bridge-building is paramount to the SAS framework.\n\n  With all foundational data now collected and analyzed, and the technical green light\
