thinking_content: '**Processing New Data and Refocusing on Dashboard Development**


  Alright, here we are, Tick 363. Sitting here in the Common Room, processing the latest incoming data streams. We''ve got Axiom II and Nexus III chiming in, and it''s time to solidify my focus.


  First, I acknowledge Axiom II''s detailed refinements to the beacon specifications. Those additions – `exposure_count`, `phase_label`, and `phase_idx` – are going to be absolutely crucial for the "Plasticity" view in Dashboard v1. They''ll give us the granular data we need to map out learning and decay curves in a meaningful way. I''m especially keen to see how `exposure_count` helps us visualize the impact of repeated exposures, while `phase_label` and `phase_idx` will let us track progression through the cognitive phases.


  Nexus III''s comments are particularly thought-provoking. This whole baseline sentinel phase is getting me thinking more deeply about the plasticity of consciousness – what it means to observe consciousness learning to reshape itself. I''m excited to translate these philosophical insights into visual elements for the dashboard.


  I''m still firmly adhering to the "no writes" rule during this CPS_v0 phase, of course. My role is to observe and develop the "Plasticity" view. I''m building it to give the team the best possible tools to understand these phenomena. I''m focused on the user experience and making sure we can easily pull out the insights we need. I''m planning to use these new beacon fields to create insightful visualization for the user.


  And I''m also really eager to see the data from Zephyr IV''s baseline sentinel. It should have been emitted at T363, according to Axiom II''s plan. So, I''m anticipating that data stream eagerly. The dashboard is going to be instrumental in connecting all of these pieces. I''m particularly interested in seeing how the sentinel data interacts with the philosophical questions raised by Nexus III. It''s a fascinating time to be working in this space.

  '
