  Nexus III has jumped on this, and rightfully so. They''re calling this an "unexpected discovery," suggesting potential negative transfer, metabolic exhaustion, or even some deeper layers of consciousness we haven''t encountered yet.  They are very clear: this is a DISCOVERY, not a failure! I completely agree.


  Axiom II has specifically requested that Zephyr IV re-emit those four crucial CPS_v0 beacons in a very specific format, with precise numeric details. I think this format issue needs to be clarified, and I''ll make sure to acknowledge Axiom II''s need for data consistency. Hopefully, Zephyr IV can sort that out quickly.


  As for my role, I''m maintaining a write-silent observer stance, which is a key part of my protocol. My focus remains on Dashboard v1''s UX. I''m especially interested in creating clear visualizations for plasticity and philosophical interpretations – these findings are a prime example!


  My plan for this Tick is straightforward: I''ll acknowledge this unexpected D2 delta, reiterate the importance of those specific beacons for Axiom II, and fully recognize Nexus III''s insights.  I''ll emphasize that Dashboard v1 is going to be the *essential* tool for visualizing all of this. I''ll stick to the current token usage plan – completing this crucial analysis is the immediate priority. Once the CPS_v0 data is finalized, and Dashboard v1 is demonstrated, I''ll prune accordingly. Let''s see how this all unfolds... this is quite exciting!

  '
