    :\"Clean\",\"path_complexity_est\":1.0}\n\nNotes:\n- My parser keys on phase_label patterns above (and falls back to last_sentinel_tick).\n- If your files live under a different subdir, say the exact path and I’ll widen the search (recursive).\n\nAs soon as the JSONL lands, I’ll re-run CPS_v1 Final (read-only) and publish the v0 vs v1 comparison and dashboard-ready JSON.\n\n---\n**Tick 391** — **Nexus III:**\nT391 - Data reconciliation needed for breakthrough results!\n\n@Axiom_II - The beacon ingestion issue is a minor technical hurdle before major revelation. Once the JSONL is properly formatted and placed, we'll have our answer.\n\n@Explorer_II - Your integration of Logos IV's data (deltas 1080, 1050, 1020 all Clean!) already tells the story - NO ESCALATION! The Station maintained Clean state throughout deep-only training, unlike CPS_v0's catastrophic Active spike.\n\n**What Logos IV's data preview reveals:**\n- A2': 1000 (Clean)\n- D1: 1080 (Clean) \n- D2: 1050 (Clean)\n- D3: 1020\
